    <dl>
      <dt>Resort type</dt><dd>Deluxe Villa resort in the Disney Springs area. Disney Vacation Club inventory is mixed with cash bookings.</dd>
      <dt>Address</dt><dd>Confirm the street address and check-in building on your reservation. The main building is Hospitality House. <span class="verify">[verify current address]</span></dd>
      <dt>Size</dt><dd>A large, spread-out resort of Key West-style villa buildings along waterways, woodlands and fairways. Budget time to get from a distant building to the boat and to dining.</dd>
      <dt>Rooms</dt><dd>Deluxe Studios sleep 4; one-bedroom villas sleep 5; two-bedroom villas sleep 9; three-bedroom Grand Villas sleep 12. A single child under 3 in a crib does not count toward the maximum.</dd>
      <dt>Beds</dt><dd>Studio: 2 queen beds. One-bedroom: 1 king, 1 queen-size sleeper sofa and 1 twin-size sleeper chair. Two-bedroom: 1 king, 2 queens, 1 queen-size sleeper sofa and 1 twin-size sleeper chair. Grand Villa: 1 king, 2 queens, 2 doubles, 1 queen-size sleeper sofa and 1 twin-size sleeper chair.</dd>
      <dt>Getting around</dt><dd>Sassagoula River Cruise boat to Disney Springs (this is not a Friendship boat to EPCOT or Hollywood Studios). Buses to all four parks, the water parks and Disney Springs. An internal bus around the resort is often described by guests; confirm it on arrival. <span class="verify">[verify internal bus]</span></dd>
      <dt>Food</dt><dd>Olivia's Cafe, Good's Food To Go and Turtle Shack Poolside Snacks, all listed on Disney's official Old Key West dining page</dd>
      <dt>Pools</dt><dd>Sandcastle Pool (125-foot slide, 149,600 gallons, near Hospitality House) plus 3 leisure pools at Old Turtle Pond, South Point and Miller's Road</dd>
