  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Old Key West is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who want more space than a Moderate hotel room, at a lower Deluxe Villa rack range than the monorail villas.</strong> In 2026 a Deluxe Studio ran about $500 to $845 a night at full price, tax included.</li>
      <li><strong>Groups using a two-bedroom or a Grand Villa,</strong> especially if a boat to Disney Springs matters more than a walk to a theme park.</li>
      <li><strong>People who don't mind a spread-out resort</strong> and will plan the walk or internal ride from a far building.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need a fifth bed in a studio.</strong> Official 2026 listings cap the Deluxe Studio at four adults, with two queen beds and no pull-down listed.</li>
      <li><strong>You thought the boat went to EPCOT or Hollywood Studios.</strong> Official water-transportation listings put Old Key West on the Sassagoula River Cruise to Disney Springs, not on the Friendship line.</li>
      <li><strong>A short walk to a park is the main reason you're booking a Deluxe.</strong> All four parks are buses from here.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
  </section>

